WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.110
Every company runs on tables.

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.810
Orders, customers, invoices, events.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.330
Thousands of them,

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.930
in databases, warehouses and folders of files.

5
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.970
And data decays quietly.

6
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.870
An order for a customer who doesn't exist.

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.210
An IBAN with a broken check digit.

8
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.250
A load that stopped in the night.

9
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.630
Most tables were never tested,

10
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.030
so nobody notices.

11
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.550
This is Sahifa.

12
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.950
From the Arabic for a written sheet:

13
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.530
the charter of Medina, which set down what each party could expect of the others.

14
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.050
Sahifa does the same for your data.

15
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:42.050
Point it at a Postgres database or a folder of files.

16
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.430
It profiles every column, writes the checks for you,

17
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.510
thirty kinds, from foreign keys to freshness,

18
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.290
and scores what it finds.

19
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.310
It only ever reads.

20
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.650
Every score comes with an honest error bar.

21
00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.990
A score from a sample tells you how sure it is, so you can tell a real drop from noise.

22
00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.330
And every finding explains itself:

23
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.110
how many rows, examples with personal values masked,

24
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.030
the SQL that found them, and what to do next.

25
00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.380
What to expect?

26
00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.140
Sahifa runs on your own machine, in about fifteen minutes.

27
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.360
It never writes to your data, and it tells you if its login could.

28
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.740
It's open source, and in preview.

29
00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.520
Test users are welcome.

30
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.210
Sahifa.

31
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.170
Know what your data promises,

32
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.870
and whether it keeps it.
